    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nForkin Earls Property are delighted to present No. 34 St. Michael's Terrace to the market. Extending to approximately 67 sq. m. (721 sq. ft.), this charming two-bedroom residence offers bright and well-proportioned accommodation, complemented by a generous private rear garden. The garden benefits from double-gated vehicular access, opening onto a convenient laneway.\n\nIdeally positioned within a mature residential setting, the property enjoys exceptional convenience, with Arklow Town Centre and an excellent range of amenities all within a short stroll.\n\nThe accommodation has been thoughtfully arranged to provide comfortable and practical living, comprising a welcoming living room with feature stove, a spacious kitchen, two bedrooms and a family bathroom. To the rear, the enclosed garden provides a wonderful outdoor retreat with ample space for al fresco dining, entertaining guests or simply relaxing in a private setting and has rear gated access.\n\nNo. 34 St. Michael's Terrace enjoys a superb location within walking distance of everything Arklow has to offer. A wide selection of supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools, bars and local shops are all close by, while the picturesque Arklow Harbour, South Beach and the renowned Arklow Golf Links are just moments from the property. Excellent transport links further enhance its appeal, with Arklow Train Station, regular bus services and the M11 motorway all within easy reach, providing straightforward access to Dublin, Wexford and beyond.\n\nCombining a highly convenient location with well-appointed accommodation and excellent outdoor space, this attractive home is sure to appeal to a wide range of purchasers, including first-time buyers, those seeking to downsize and investors looking to acquire a quality property in a well-established residential area.\n\nViewing is highly recommended and is strictly by appointment."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nLiving Room - 4.88m x 4.07m\nThe bright and spacious living room enjoys an abundance of natural light from its front-facing window and is centred around a solid fuel stove, creating a warm and cosy atmosphere. This comfortable reception room offers ample space for both relaxing and entertaining.\n\nKicthen/Dining Room - 3.88m x 3.93m\nPositioned to the rear of the property, the generously proportioned kitchen/dining room is flooded with natural light from two large Velux roof windows. Fitted with an extensive range of wall and floor cabinets, it offers excellent storage and workspace, while providing ample room for family dining and everyday living.\n\nRear gallery kitchen - 3.39m x 1.76m\nLocated just off the main kitchen, the rear kitchen provides additional preparation space and direct access to the rear garden, making it ideal for busy family life.\n\nUtility Space - 1.33m x 2.20m\nThe separate utility room provides additional storage and dedicated laundry facilities, adding to the practicality and functionality of the home.\n\nBathroom - 1.97m x 2.20m\nSituated on the ground floor, the bathroom is conveniently located off the utility room and is fitted with a bath, wash hand basin and WC.\n\nBedroom 1 - 1.12m x 4.07m\nA generous double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, offering laminate wooden flooring and ample space for freestanding furniture.\n\nBedroom 2 - 1.71m x 4.07m\nA well-proportioned second bedroom offering flexibility as a guest room, children's bedroom or home office, with views to the front of the property.\n\nRear Garden - \nTo the rear, the property enjoys a generous, enclosed garden laid mainly in lawn with mature shrubs and planting. Offering excellent privacy and plenty of outdoor space, it is ideal for children, gardening enthusiasts or those wishing to create an outdoor entertaining area. A garden has gated pedestrian access and a shed which provides additional external storage.\n\nIncluded in the Sale - \n• Floor coverings, curtains, integrated cooker and dishwasher.\n\nServices - \n• Oil fired central heating.• Mains water, electricity and sewage.• Telephone and broadband available in the area.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Bright and well-proportioned two-bedroom mid-terrace residence extending to approximately 67 sq.m. (721 sq.ft.)</li><li> Spacious kitchen/dining room with Velux roof windows complimented by a separate utility room offering additional practicality.</li><li> Double glazed windows throughout.</li><li> Large enclosed rear garden with excellent outdoor space and pedestrian gated access.</li><li> Conveniently located within walking distance of Arklow town centre and a wide range of local amenities including, shops, schools, harbour, beach, golf club, main street shopping, and all town facilities. Excellent transport links nearby, including Arklow Train Station and the M11 motorway.</ul>"
      },
